{"gene":"SOCS1","uniprot":"O15524","proteinName":"suppressor of cytokine signaling 1","function":"Essential negative regulator of type I and type II interferon (IFN) signaling, as well as that of other cytokines, including IL2, IL4, IL6 and leukemia inhibitory factor (LIF). Downregulates cytokine signaling by inhibiting the JAK/STAT signaling pathway. Acts by binding to JAK proteins and to IFNGR1 and inhibiting their kinase activity. In vitro, suppresses Tec protein-tyrosine activity. Regulates IFN-gamma (IFNG)-mediated sensory neuron survival. Probable substrate recognition component of an ECS (Elongin BC-CUL2/5-SOCS-box protein) E3 ubiquitin ligase complex which mediates the ubiquitination and subsequent proteasomal degradation of target proteins","pathwayComment":"Protein modification; protein ubiquitination","pathways":[{"id":"R-HSA-1280218","name":"Adaptive Immune System","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-983168","name":"Antigen processing: Ubiquitination & Proteasome degradation","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-983169","name":"Class I MHC mediated antigen processing & presentation","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-1280215","name":"Cytokine Signaling in Immune system","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-982772","name":"Growth hormone receptor signaling","evidence":"IEA","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9705462","name":"Inactivation of CSF3 (G-CSF) signaling","evidence":"IEA","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-168249","name":"Innate Immune System","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-909733","name":"Interferon alpha/beta signaling","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-877300","name":"Interferon gamma signaling","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-913531","name":"Interferon Signaling","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-6785807","name":"Interleukin-4 and Interleukin-13 signaling","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false}